      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Not a massive field for the big one of the day, the famous My Wycheproof Cup, but a competitive affair. SEA STRIKE (2) appeals in this company after a cracker of a return run in a heat of the MCC Series at Geelong, when beaten just over a length and a half. Great effort first-up at 1700m, so should have taken great improvement from that. SCALEXTRICS (4) made his debut for Taige Weir in the Avoca Cup and found only one better, so with the benefit of that you'd think he'll be better here. If that's the right form you've got respect MANGIONE (3), who was just behind SCALEXTRICS at Avoca and won the Coleraine Cup the start prior. SWITCH HIT (5) is rising in grade but has been right around the mark in recent starts and won't disgrace himself. Similar story with PALTINIAN (8) who beaten only 1-1/4 lengths last start after a photo finish defeat second-up. Ready for a peak run now.",
